# JSDoc type imports (checkJs)

Runtime code is plain `.js` with `checkJs`. Import types for JSDoc **once at the top** of the file — never inline `import('…')` inside `@typedef`, `@param`, `@property`, or `@type`.

## Pattern

```js
import { loadEnvGraphForDir } from '@qctl/shared'

/** @import { EnvGraph } from '@qctl/shared' */
/** @import { Argv } from 'yargs' */

/** @typedef {ReturnType<typeof loadEnvGraphForDir>} LoadedGraph */
```

Place `@import` comments immediately after runtime `import` statements (before `@typedef` blocks and implementation).

## One `@import` per module

When several types come from the **same module**, use a **single** `@import` comment — not multiple comments for the same `from '…'`.

Named imports inside the braces are **lexicographically sorted** (ASCII, case-sensitive).

```js
// GOOD — merged, sorted
/** @import { InitProfile, PlatformStage, QctlRole } from '@qctl/shared' */

// BAD — split across duplicate module specifiers
/** @import { InitProfile } from '@qctl/shared' */
/** @import { PlatformStage } from '@qctl/shared' */
```

Sort `@import` blocks themselves by Biome `organizeImports` groups (`node:` → packages → `@qctl/*` → `#` → relative), then specifier localeCompare.

Use a multiline `@import` when the sorted list exceeds the line width (100).

## Do

- `/** @import { SyncOptions } from './sync.js' */` then use `SyncOptions` in JSDoc
- `ReturnType<typeof fn>` when `fn` is a **runtime** import
- Local `@typedef` only for aliases composed from imported names

## Don't

```js
// BAD — inline import() in JSDoc
/** @typedef {import('./sync.js').SyncOptions} SyncOptions */
/** @param {import('yargs').Argv} argv */
```

## Runtime dynamic import()

`await import('module')` for lazy loading is fine — this rule applies only to **type-only** JSDoc annotations, not runtime imports.
